{% extends "_layouts/default.njk" %}

{% set title = false %}

{% block content %}
  <div class="nhsuk-grid-row">
    <div class="nhsuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      {% if session %}
        {{ heading({
          text: __("consent.start.title." + session.presetNames[0])
        }) }}

        {% for programme in session.programmes %}
          {% if session.programmes.length != 1 %}
            <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-m">{{ programme.title }}</h2>
          {% endif %}

          {{ programme.information.startPage | nhsukMarkdown }}

          {{ link(programme.information.url, __("consent.start.more", { programme: programme })) | nhsukMarkdown }}
        {% endfor %}

        <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-m">
          {{ __("consent.start.confirm.title") }}
        </h2>

        {{ button({
          text: __("consent.start.confirm.buttonText"),
          href: session.consentUrl + "/new"
        }) }}

        <h3 class="nhsuk-heading-s">
          {{ __("consent.start.otherMethods.title") }}
        </h3>

        {{ __("consent.start.otherMethods.description") | nhsukMarkdown }}
      {% else %}
        {{ heading({
          text: serviceName
        }) }}

        {% filter nhsukMarkdown %}
Instead of relying on paper forms sent home in school bags, we’re contacting parents and carers directly via email or text message.

If your local NHS vaccination team uses this service, you’ll get an email or text message with a link to an online consent form when your child is due their next vaccination.

You can use the online form to:
- give consent for your child to be vaccinated at school
- say you do not want your child to be vaccinated at school, or on the date proposed
- ask for more information

Find out more about the [school age vaccination schedule on the NHS website](https://www.nhs.uk/vaccinations/nhs-vaccinations-and-when-to-have-them/).
        {% endfilter %}
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
{% endblock %}
